We sampled files for 40 out of 182 classes from the xeno-canto-additional dataset and cropped the segments where the birds were vocalizing to create a clean dataset. We sampled audio files containing only background noise (without bird calls) from the unlabeled soundscape dataset. We combined the clean dataset and background noise to create a test-like dataset with time-series labels. Using this synthetic dataset, we calculated the ROC AUC score. Although this validation method did not perfectly correlate with the LB results, it provided more reasonable outcomes compared to using the first 5-second crop method. For more details, please refer to this notebook.
TTA To enhance the accuracy of our time series predictions, we employed techniques similar to sub-pixel super-resolution. Instead of predicting just the 5-second frames during inference, we also predicted frames shifted by 2.5 seconds. We then combined these results as a TTA. This method helped in refining the overall predictions.
